            "The rule mirrors what process capability indices express: Six Sigma's Cpk falls either because the mean sits too close to the limit or because the spread is too wide, and the two causes need different remedies. Moving the mean usually means removing delay or effort; narrowing the spread usually means finding and removing specific causes of variation.",
            TIP("Do not choose by preference or by which belt your organisation already trained. Write the requirement, plot the actual results against it, and let the shape of the data decide where to start."),
